    "title": "Patrick Mahomes and Tom Brady: A Historic Super Bowl Showdown",
    "text": "• Patrick Mahomes can become the first quarterback in NFL history to win three consecutive Super Bowls.\n• Tom Brady has won seven Super Bowls, six with the New England Patriots and one with the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.\n• Brady joined Fox Sports as a commentator with a 10-year contract worth £300 million.\n• This is Brady's first season as a commentator, and he replaced Greg Olsen as the main co-commentator.\n• Brady has a five percent ownership stake in the Las Vegas Raiders, affecting his commentary role.\n• Mahomes and the Kansas City Chiefs have won the last two Super Bowls, defeating the Philadelphia Eagles and the San Francisco 49ers.\n• If Mahomes wins this Sunday, the Super Bowl count between him and Brady could narrow to 7-4.\n• Brady and the Patriots never achieved three consecutive Super Bowl wins.\n• The Chiefs' success is attributed to their coach Andy Reid, defensive coordinator Steve Spagnuolo, and key players like Chris Jones and Trent McDuffie.\n• Patrick Mahomes was drafted in 2017 and has shown exceptional skills as a quarterback.\n• Mahomes is under 30 years old and plays in a league where elite quarterbacks often continue until 40.\n• The Philadelphia Eagles are considered a stronger team than the one that lost to Brady two years ago.\n• The Chiefs have consistently found ways to win close games this season.",
